[start-outcomes] After this part you should be able to
1. explain why the moment in a slender column grows by itself, and find the second-order moment M_2 by nominal curvature in six steps, with creep (K_φ ) and the axial-load factor K_r ;
2. find the design moment of a braced slender column from its four candidates, or of an unbraced one from M_{02} + M_2 , and iterate K_r with the steel;
3. decide with the screening of EC2 5.8.9(3) whether a column needs a biaxial check, and carry it out with the enhanced moment and Eq. 5.39, taking the imperfection in one direction at a time;
4. complete the design of a column about both axes, and find the slips in someone else’s nominal-curvature calculation.
